{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/library/11776","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"call number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300311706"}],"content":"PS3515.A795 T8","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":"11776","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Twenty-five poems. ","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[{"_label":"Marsden Hartley","id":"actor/hartley-marsden","type":"Actor"},{"_label":"Contact Pub. Co.","id":"actor/contact-pub-co","type":"Actor"}],"timespan":{"_label":"1923","begin_of_the_begin":"1923-01-01T00:00:00Z","end_of_the_end":"1923-01-01T00:00:00Z","type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"Ephemera found inside front cover : Intimate Gallery flyer announcing the exhibition Twenty Sculptures by Gaston Lachaise, 1927.\nEphemera found inside front cover : Handwritten list of edits for publication by [Alfred Stieglitz?].\nGeorgia O'Keeffe Personal Library.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"inscription statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435414"}],"content":"abq copies : fair condition.|SColl abq 03:03-14 : Annotation by unknown : pp. 5 ; 12 ; 32 ; 34 ; 36 ; 47 ; 50 ; 54 ; 58.|SColl abq 03:03-14 : Inscription on t.p. from Marsden Hartley to Alfred Stieglitz, September 27, 1923 : Dear Stieglitz. / This is the other angle / of me - another outcome / of that telling day in 1908 / when you said - I don't / say I understand your / paintings but I'd like to / give you a show. It was / in the then gossipy 291 when / only Parisian sensations were / called authentic by these who / have since been but faintly heard / from. Mary Shaw said to me once / the Yankees are wonderful 'when / they go to the other way'. Well the / other way is longest but most / exciting. / Devotion as always / Marsden Hartley. / Berlin - Sep 27 - 1923..|SColl abq 03:03-15 : Annotation by Alfred Stieglitz or unknown : pp. 4 ; 12 ; 34 ; 47 ; 50.|SColl abq 03:03-15 : Embossed stamp on front loose endpaper : Georgia O'Keeffe / Abiquiu, New Mexico.|SColl abq 03:03-15 : Signature on t.p. by Marsden Hartley.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}